{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdyb45LPFJBh3TsjL6y8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xft8C2KXao5NPW7zNzSLHg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T212815.394084Z-047b77ac3a/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/newly_discovered_d13_layout_versioning_defect.txt","content":"Newly discovered defect, found only because P-N31-001's wiring makes a real\nrepair-and-retest loop reachable for the first time: `nodes/render.py`'s\nD13_RENDER_UNIT stamps every layout render's `version` from\n\n    current = heads.get(layout_stream) or {}\n    version_record = {..., \"version\": current.get(\"version\", 0) + 1, ...}\n\n(`runtime/langgraph_factory/nodes/render.py`, D13_RENDER_UNIT, the\n`version_record` construction around line 102-106) -- but the \"layout\" stream\nis never written into `artifact_heads` anywhere in this file (confirmed: no\n`advance_head`/`artifact_heads[...]` write for \"layout\" in render.py). It is,\nby design, an append-only versioned stream, not head-tracked -- exactly what\n`repair.py`'s own `_current_parent()` docstring already documents (\"layout\ndoes not [advance through artifact_heads]\").\n\nConsequence: `heads.get(layout_stream)` is always `{}`, so *every* D13 render\ncall -- the unit's first render, and any later retest render -- stamps\n`version = 1`. This was never observable before D16-D23 were wired (P-N90's\nfinding F1): nothing had ever called D13 a second time for the same unit in\na real run.\n\n`repair.D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR`, by contrast, versions its own admitted\ndeterministic-repair child correctly, from `repair._current_parent()`'s\nreal-candidate-only scan of `artifact_versions` (`current_version + 1`, i.e.\n`version = 2` after one real render). Once a layout repair is admitted, its\nrecord legitimately outranks the *next* real D13 render (which is buggily\nstill `version = 1`) under `nodes.latest_candidate()`'s plain\nhighest-version selection (`runtime/langgraph_factory/nodes/__init__.py`,\n`latest_candidate`) -- so a subsequent D14 call resolves the *admitted repair\nrecord* (`body`-nested, no top-level `pdf_sha256`) as \"the current layout\nversion\" instead of the fresher real render, and fails closed:\n\n    SystemFailure(\"integrity\", \"the layout version has no PDF hash\")\n\nReproduced deterministically by\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py::\ntest_a_layout_finding_drives_a_real_d17_through_d21_loop_back_toward_d16`,\nwhich asserts this exact, current, correct-per-existing-code behavior (not a\nhoped-for fix) -- see that test's own docstring for the full trace.\n\nScope: `nodes/render.py` and `nodes/__init__.py::latest_candidate` are not in\nN31's write set (N22's). This finding is reported here, not patched, the same\nway N90's own audit reported F1 for N31 to fix via a later patch cycle\n(P-N31-001) -- a future patch should route this to whichever node owns\n`nodes/render.py` (N22) to fix D13's layout version-stamping to read from\n`_current_parent`-style real-candidate scanning instead of `artifact_heads`.\n\nBlast radius if unfixed: any *second* call to D13_RENDER_UNIT for the same\nunit within one episode -- a layout repair-and-retest loop (spec section\n8.2/12, the \"unit layout\" owner), or a crash-recovery replay that re-enters\nD13 -- will misresolve \"the current layout version\" once a higher-versioned\nnon-render record (a deterministic repair child, or in future any other\nrecord minted against the layout stream) exists. It does not affect the D16\nPASS fast path (a unit whose first render and inspection already pass never\ncalls D13 twice) or any other owner's repair loop (no other owner's retest\nchain re-enters D13 before D16 without D14 resetting the layout stream's\nversion bookkeeping the same way).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":138,"cache_read_input_tokens":244858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":138},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85ccdb45-8482-4249-a92f-e9379e0b4244","uuid":"4076b88a-8fc9-4404-8ec6-a2923f42c6a6","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:46:39.334Z","request_id":"req_011Cdyb43xHRFQvmQs1aWQ1N"}
