ore_the_terminal_write_still_lets_d98_be_invoked_cleanly`.\n\n## P-N31-001 proof verdicts (this pass)\n\n- **PASSED** — `test_d16_through_d23_are_members_of_the_real_compiled_graph`.\n- **PASSED** — `test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges`.\n- **PASSED** — `test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_the_repair_acceptance_widening`.\n- **PASSED** — `test_register_skeleton_does_not_raise_against_the_widened_bindings`.\n- **PASSED** — `test_a_clean_unit_reaches_unit_accepted_through_the_real_compiled_graph`\n  (D16 PASS fast path, real compiled graph, real `UNIT_ACCEPTED`).\n- **PASSED** — `test_a_layout_finding_drives_a_real_d17_through_d21_loop_back_toward_d16`\n  (real D17-D21 loop, real retest dispatch; does not itself reach a second\n  passing D16 — see \"Newly discovered defect\" above).\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N32 and future generations)\n\n- The deterministic-vs-model routing table for `source interpretation` is\n  simplified to always route to M06 in this generation; spec section 12\n  allows a deterministic refetch when a locator remains authorized, which\n  would require a source-retrieval integration this node's write set does\n  not include (`repair.py`'s module docstring records the reasoning).\n- `compute_unit_denominator()`'s coverage of spec section 13.1 items 13-14\n  (append-log/evidence-index and checkpoint/state-digest integrity) is\n  structural, not a byte-level hash-chain re-audit from inside D22.\n- **New this pass**: `nodes/render.py`'s D13 layout version-stamping (not in\n  this node's write set) blocks a real layout repair-and-retest loop from\n  ever reaching a second, passing D16 — see \"Newly discovered defect\" above\n  and `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/newly_discovered_d13_layout_versioning_defect.txt`.\n- **New this pass**: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` carries 2\n  residual failures this node cannot fix from its own write set — see\n  \"Residual test_plan26_unit_graph.py failures\" above.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5713,"cache_read_input_tokens":246812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5713},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85ccdb45-8482-4249-a92f-e9379e0b4244","uuid":"e8a5d744-6ed2-4b29-8e8a-03af170fa876","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:48:07.751Z","request_id":"req_011Cdyb5rWmKDUftgdUMAZvg"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UwfFnZm8Y4RnjRpvJLnmEP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T212815.394084Z-047b77ac3a/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85ccdb45-8482-4249-a92f-e9379e0b4244","uuid":"e521831b-910b-45d6-b342-dd50a341c592","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:48:07.807Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T212815.394084Z-047b77ac3a/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md","content":"# N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE result\n\nstatus: BLOCKED\nnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md\npredecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\ngeneration: 2 (P-N31-001, P-N31-002 applied)\n\n## Why BLOCKED, not PASSED\n\nEvery one of this node's own TEST 1-10 items passes (38/38 in\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py`, including the new\nP-N31-001 compiled-graph proof tests), and P-N31-001's required proof is\nfully met with real compiled-graph evidence (see below). Per P-N31-002's own\ninstruction, though, this report's status must reflect both required\nverification commands, and one of them does not come back clean:\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` — required by P-N31-001 specifically\nso a regression here would be caught before merge — still fails 2 of 93\ntests, for reasons that are a direct, structural consequence of D16-D23 now\nbeing wired (exactly what P-N31-001 asked for), in a file outside this\nnode's declared writable paths. P-N31-002 is explicit: *\"If\n`test_plan26_unit_graph.py` still fails for a reason unrelated to what\nN20/N30 already fixed, report that honestly rather than adjusting the status\nline to PASSED anyway.\"* That is exactly this situation (detail below), so\nthis report says so rather than marking PASSED.\n\n## P-N31-001 correction: D16-D23 wired into the one production compiled graph\n\nN90's independent audit (finding F1) found D16-D23 fully implemented and\nfunction-level tested (this node's own generation-1 TEST 1-10, all passing)\nbut never registered into `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` — a real run\ncould never reach `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED` for any unit, because\ngeneration 1's own docstrings deferred that wiring to N32, whose own prompt\ndeferred it right back. P-N31-001 puts `graph.py` in this node's write set to\nclose that gap here, as the node that owns the repair/acceptance node bodies.\n\n**What changed in `graph.py`** (already present in this generation's working\ntree when this pass began; this pass's job was verifying and proving it, not\nauthoring it from scratch): `UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` (D16-D23 mapped to their\nreal `acceptance`/`repair` callables), `UNIT_REPAIR_BRANCHES` (the eight\nconditional-edge/guard-function pairs of spec 8.2's repair/acceptance cycle),\n`register_unit_repair_path()` (wires those edges additively over a builder\nthat already has the skeleton and unit path — the same pattern\n`workbook.register_workbook_path` established), `repair_acceptance_bindings()`\n(`binding_inventory()` plus D16-D23, kept as a separate function precisely so\n`binding_inventory()`'s own return value — which several of N30's frozen\ntests independently recompute their expectations from — stays byte-identical)\nand `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` now compiling against\n`repair_acceptance_bindings()` instead of the narrower `binding_inventory()`.\n`unit_graph.py` itself is untouched, exactly as P-N31-001 requires: widening\nthe `available` sequence `register_unit_path` receives is what resolves the\nsix N31-owned `DEFERRED_EDGES` rows automatically, which is `unit_graph.py`'s\nown pre-existing, already-correct machinery.\n\n**Required proof, added this pass** to\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` (none of this existed before\nthis pass — generation 1's own report said \"this generation does not add or\nedit a line of `graph.py`\"; the code above was present but unverified when\nthis pass began):\n\n- `test_d16_through_d23_are_members_of_the_real_compiled_graph` — asserts all\n  eight against `build_curriculum_factory_graph(...).get_graph().nodes`\n  (`G.compiled_topology`), the same check N90's own audit used.\n- `test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges` — asserts\n  each of the six N31-owned `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows is a real edge\n  of the compiled graph's own edge list, and that `unit_graph.\n  branch_destinations`/`deferred_destinations`, asked against the widened\n  `repair_acceptance_bindings()` set, agree (destination present, not\n  deferred).\n- `test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_the_repair_acceptance_widening`\n  — asserts `binding_inventory()` stays free of D16-D23 and that\n  `repair_acceptance_bindings() - binding_inventory() == {D16..D23}` exactly.\n- `test_register_skeleton_does_not_raise_against_the_widened_bindings` —\n  calls `register_skeleton` directly over a fresh `StateGraph` with\n  `repair_acceptance_bindings()`; no `GraphBindingError`/`UnitTopologyError`.\n- `test_a_clean_unit_reaches_unit_accepted_through_the_real_compiled_graph` —\n  a real `compiled.stream(...)` run (real `FakeCliTransport`, scripted M0x\n  responses, adapted from `test_plan26_adversarial.py`'s own harness pattern)\n  reaches `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT` and a real\n  `accepted_unit_receipts[UNIT]` (D16 PASS fast path).\n- `test_a_layout_finding_drives_a_real_d17_through_d21_loop_back_toward_d16` —\n  a real, organically-produced D14 `layout_repairable` finding traverses\n  D17 → D18 → D19 (deterministic route) → D20 → D21, which dispatches retest\n  to `D13_RENDER_UNIT` — the full internal D17-D21 cycle, for real, over the\n  compiled graph's real conditional edges. See \"Newly discovered defect\"\n  below for why this run does not itself reach a second, passing D16.\n\nCompiled-graph evidence (node list, six wired edges, `binding_inventory()`\ndiff): `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_proof.txt`.\n\n## Newly discovered defect: `nodes/render.py` D13 layout version-stamping\n\n`test_a_layout_finding_drives_a_real_d17_through_d21_loop_back_toward_d16`\nproves the D17-D21 wiring and internal topology are correct and reachable,\nbut the run does not converge back to a passing D16 in the same episode: the\nretest's own second `D13_RENDER_UNIT` call stamps `version = 1` for the\nlayout stream every time (`heads.get(layout_stream)` is always empty — layout\nis documented as append-only-versioned, not head-tracked, and D13 never\nwrites it into `artifact_heads`), so the fresh real render loses to D20's own\n(correctly-versioned) admitted repair record under `nodes.latest_candidate`'s\nplain highest-version selection. The retest's D14 call then fails closed\n(`\"the layout version has no PDF hash\"`) instead of reaching D16.\n\nThis is a genuine, newly discovered defect in `nodes/render.py` (N22's write,\nnot in this node's write set) that only a real D16-D23-wired run could ever\nexpose — the exact kind of finding N90's own audit produced for this node,\nnow produced by this node for N22. Full root-cause writeup:\n`results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/newly_discovered_d13_layout_versioning_defect.txt`.\nNot patched here, per the LOOP's own instruction (\"Route any D98 defect back\nto N22; do not write terminal code here\") and this node's write set.\n\n## Residual `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` failures (2 of 93)\n\nRe-run against the current tree (D16-D23 now really wired):\n`results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/unit_graph_verification_run.txt`.\nBoth failures are direct, structural consequences of the wiring correction,\nin a file **not** in this node's declared writable paths\n(`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` is absent from\n`[\"runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py\", \"runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py\",\n\"runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py\", \"tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py\",\n\"plans/.../N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md\", \"plans/.../evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\"]`),\nso this pass does not edit it:\n\n- `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` — its own\n  docstring already predicts this exact failure and names N31 as the owner of\n  the rewrite (\"Once N31 wires D16-D23 that premise inverts... this test is\n  expected to start failing at that point, and rewriting it then is N31's...\n  to do\"), deliberately left un-widened by P-N30-001 (unlike five sibling\n  tests P-N30-001 did fix). The test's whole premise — that M05's own update\n  is unobservable because the M05→D16 edge is deferred — is now false by\n  construction: M05's update is observable (real state, real trace) once D16\n  has a real body. This is the pipeline behaving correctly (P-N30-001's own\n  words for the sibling case), not a regression.\n- `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`\n  — P-N30-001 *did* widen this test's assumption (its docstring already notes\n  the clean episode \"legitimately loops back to a second `D05` call\"), but the\n  fix has a residual gap: independently reproduced (outside pytest, streaming\n  the same fixture directly), the clean one-unit episode really does call\n  `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` a second time and really does correctly clear\n  `selected_unit_id` (`pending_guard` persists as `{\"node\":\n  \"D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT\", \"value\": \"manifest_exhausted\", ...}`, `cursor`\n  correctly shows `accepted_ordinal: 1`) before correctly halting on the\n  still-deferred `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE` row. But that second\n  `D05` call's own update chunk is never yielded by\n  `compiled.stream(stream_mode=\"updates\")` before the `KeyError` for the\n  unregistered `D24` destination is raised — LangGraph resolves the next\n  step's routing (and raises there) in the same tick it would otherwise yield\n  the just-completed step's chunk, so the second `D05` call is invisible to\n  `result[\"trace\"]` even though it is real and checkpointed. The test's\n  `d05_calls = result[\"trace\"].count(\"D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT\")` therefore reads\n  `1` in the exhausted case, not `2`, so its `if d05_calls == 1: assert\n  state[\"selected_unit_id\"] == \"U001\"` branch is taken and fails against the\n  correctly-cleared `None`. This is a stream/exception-interaction artifact of\n  the test harness's own trace collection, not a defect in `graph.py`,\n  `repair.py`, or `acceptance.py` — nothing in this node's write set can\n  change how `compiled.stream()` batches an update chunk against a\n  same-tick routing `KeyError`.\n\nBoth are genuine fixes this node cannot make from its own write set. Per\nP-N31-002, reported here rather than routed around.\n\n## What this node built (generation 1, unchanged this pass)\n\nTwo top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns\nrepair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):\n\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18\n  (targeted repair planning), D19 (deterministic-vs-model routing), D20\n  (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch).\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator\n  reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +\n  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage\n  predicate N32 calls.\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls every function\ndirectly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged step-to-step\nthrough the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), not a mock merge,\nfor TEST 1-10; this pass's own P-N31-001 proof section (above) additionally\ndrives the real compiled graph end to end.\n\n## Owner / retest map\n\n| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |\n| curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |\n| unit content | content | model (M06) | `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT` |\n| unit visual | visuals | model (M06) unless every named key is an authoritative/library brief, then deterministic | `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS` |\n| unit layout | layout | deterministic (boundary-scoped pointer correction) | `D13_RENDER_UNIT` |\n\n`repair.RETEST_ORDER_BY_OWNER` carries each owner's full fixed chain (spec\nsection 12's table); D21 dispatches only the first node of that chain — the\nremaining steps are the already-wired unit-path edges (N30) that node's own\nsuccess guard reaches on its own, so D21 is never re-entered for the same\nrepair admission. This pass's real compiled-graph run confirms this for the\n\"unit layout\" owner (D21 dispatches once to `D13_RENDER_UNIT`; see above).\n\nFrozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17\nowns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns\nthe numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`).\n\n## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n\nRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\nminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\nCategories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),\ndomain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content\ncheck set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join\nresult, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\nindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\nthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\nverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\nunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\nindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\nconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\nconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\nreduction (stale evidence cannot pass) without needing to delete anything —\n`compute_unit_denominator` only counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the\n*current* head. This pass's real compiled-graph run additionally proves D16\npasses for real, organically-produced state (not hand-built) on the clean\nfast path.\n\nDocumented, not silently assumed, scope limit: this generation's denominator\ntreats the append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer\nas structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\nthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\nsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this so\na future generation tightens it rather than rediscovering the gap.\n\n## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports\n`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` unmodified and calls\n`terminal.write_terminal()` directly — the identical function N22 wrote and\nN32 calls for its two product-terminal sites — never a stand-in:\n\n- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:\n  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from this generation's real D22/D23\n  output is independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own\n  `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n- `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the\n  same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes\n  `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own\n  re-derivation did.\n- `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`:\n  the `terminal_candidate` D18 proposes on attempt-bound exhaustion is\n  independently accepted by D98's `_validate_exhausted`.\n\nNo test in this file, and no code in `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`/`graph.py`,\nwrites to `nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is\nasserted to still be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`. The real\ncompiled-graph run (`test_a_layout_finding_...`) additionally proves D98 is\nreached and writes `SYSTEM_FAILURE` for a real, code-detected integrity fault\n(the D13 defect above) with no N31 code involved in that decision either.\n\n## Commands and results\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py -v\n=> 38 passed in 0.79s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -v\n=> 2 failed, 91 passed in 6.56s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/unit_graph_verification_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/ -k plan26 -q\n=> 3 failed, 1064 passed, 1 skipped, 174 deselected, 345 subtests passed\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n```\n\nThe third failure in the full-suite run,\n`test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py::\ntest_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_after_harness_or_predecessor_change`, is\nnot a required verification command for this node and reads the live\nreceipt/log store directly (`results/v3/*.receipt.v1.json`,\n`results/v3/logs/**`), which this node's declared writable paths do not\ninclude and neither `repair.py`, `acceptance.py`, `graph.py`, nor the test\nfile touches; pre-existing environment/controller-state drift, not a\nregression from this pass.\n\n## Hashes\n\n| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/l